reak of identical flips, scaled by the sequence's length. This targets the critique's significant `longest_run_coef_given_alt` finding (z = −3.5, q = 0.008): people penalise long streaks more than the alternation rate alone explains.\n\n**Check results:**\n- **ELPD-LOO:** −1081.5 on the smoke fit, against the incumbent's −1088.2. That fit was one chain of 100 draws, so this is a weak early sign, not a result.\n- **PSIS-LOO unreliable:** 5.7% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance. So the −1081.5 itself may be inaccurate, and if the full fit also comes out unreliable, the model can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Not checked:** the check doesn't test convergence (it couldn't compute R-hat from a single chain) or novelty against the live models. Admission tests both.\n- **Speed:** the smoke fit took 56 s to sample.\n\n**What I didn't address:** the critique's strongest finding was the penalty on periodic patterns (z = 6.1). I left it alone on the guess that the other incumbent-refinement slot (candidate 3) would take it. Its directory had no hypothesis yet when I looked, so that's unconfirmed.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`","ttft_ms":4579,"type":"result","duration_ms":256068,"uuid":"6c010c7e-bb49-478a-a811-6579ca286960","ttft_stream_ms":3581,"time_to_request_ms":108,"first_content_frame_ms":3582,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
